  // Combat log fragments — these are the static pieces of damage messages
  // that get concatenated with dynamic numbers (e.g. "You attack for " +
  // playerDmg + " damage."). t() does an exact-string lookup, so a message
  // built by concatenation could never match a whole-sentence key once a
  // number was mixed in — it silently fell back to English every time,
  // even with a full translation table, because the *pieces* around the
  // number had no entries of their own. This was the main dungeon's most
  // frequently seen text (fires on every single combat turn), so it was
  // the biggest visible source of "half Portuguese, half English."
